#* Path: {{headless/auto-update/update-mgmt-api/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/update/service/model/AssignVersionRequest.java}}
# *AssignDeploymentTargetsEndpoint.java* - Pass forceInstall to AssignVersionRequest
#* Path: {{commerce-central/commerce-central-deployments/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/commerce/central/deployments/service/AssignDeploymentTargetsEndpoint.java}}
# *AssignVersionEndpoint.java* - Pass force to scheduleVersion
#* Path: {{headless/auto-update/update-mgmt/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/update/service/AssignVersionEndpoint.java}}
# *InstallRepository.java* - Add force parameter and set forceFlag on TargetVersionModel
#* Path: {{headless/auto-update/update-mgmt/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/update/model/InstallRepository.java}}

----

h2. Testing

h3. Test Case 1: Force Install Enabled

# Create a deployment template with Force Install checkbox *checked*
# Assign deployment to a store group
# Check the manifest XML at the update server endpoint
# *Expected*: {{<property key="force" value="true"/>}}
# Have a store check for updates during business hours
# *Expected*: Update installs immediately

h3. Test Case 2: Force Install Disabled

# Create a deployment template with Force Install checkbox *unchecked*
# Assign deployment to a store group
# Check the manifest XML at the update server endpoint
# *Expected*: {{<property key="force" value="false"/>}}
# Have a store check for updates during business hours
# *Expected*: Update does NOT install (waits for store to close)

----

h2. Related Code References

h3. Complete Data Flow (After Fix)

{noformat}UI Checkbox (forceInstall)
    ↓
DeploymentTemplateStep (Angular Form)
    ↓
SaveDeploymentTemplateRequest
    ↓
SaveDeploymentTemplateEndpoint
    ↓
DeploymentTemplateStepModel (Database: template_step.forceInstall)
    ↓
AssignDeploymentTargetsEndpoint.writeTargets()
    ↓ template.getSteps().get(targetStep).isForceInstall()
AssignVersionRequest.force ← FIX #1: Add this field
    ↓
AssignVersionEndpoint.assignVersion()
    ↓ request.isForce() ← FIX #2: Pass this parameter
InstallRepository.scheduleVersion(force) ← FIX #3: Add parameter
    ↓ .forceFlag(force) ← FIX #4: Set this field
TargetVersionModel (Database: target_version.forceFlag)
    ↓
ManifestEndpoint.getExpectedVersion()
    ↓ version.setForce(targetVersion.isForceFlag())
ManifestEndpoint.buildConfiguration()
    ↓ .property("force", Boolean.toString(version.isForce()))
Manifest XML: <property key="force" value="true|false"/>
    ↓
Bootstrap: getResolvedProperty("force")
    ↓
ServiceRuntime: Decides whether to install during business hours{noformat}

h3. Key Database Tables

# *template_step* - Stores deployment template steps with {{forceInstall}} column
# *target_version* - Stores version assignments with {{forceFlag}} column

h3. Key API Endpoints

# *POST /api/rest/central/deployments/deployments/save* - Saves deployment templates
# *POST /api/rest/central/deployments/deployments/assign* - Assigns versions to groups
# *PUT /api/update-mgt/assign-version* - Updates management service assigns version
# *GET /api/update/manifest/{businessUnitId}/{package}* - Returns manifest XML

----

h2. Version Comparison Note

The customer mentions that this issue occurs in version 243.1, and they're comparing behavior with JDNA on version 243.8. This suggests the bug may have been introduced in 243.1 or earlier, and potentially fixed in a later version. It would be worth checking if version 243.8 or later already includes this fix.

----

h2. Additional Observations

h3. Manual Service Restart Requirement

The customer also mentions needing to manually restart the JMC service for updates to propagate. This is a separate issue from the force install flag not being set. The expected behavior is:

# *Force Install = true*: Update should install immediately during business hours
# *Force Install = false*: Update should install when the store closes (business unit open flag = false)

In both cases, no manual service restart should be required. The auto-updater should:

* Detect the new version from the manifest
* Download the update files
* Apply the update at the appropriate time (immediately if forced, or at store close)
* Restart the service automatically

If manual restarts are required even after this fix is applied, there may be additional issues with the auto-updater installation process itself.

----

h2. Conclusion

The Force Install feature is not working because the {{forceInstall}} value from the deployment template is never propagated to the {{TargetVersionModel}} in the database. The fix requires adding the force flag to the {{AssignVersionRequest}} model and ensuring it flows through the entire assignment chain from the deployment template to the target version model.

This is a straightforward data flow issue with a clear, surgical fix requiring changes to 4 files.

