Description:
When {{openpos.devices.enableMobilePrint}} is disabled, the printer is not working.  We are getting a ‘Failed to Print’ dialog (image-20250916-145518.png).  Previously, the cash drawer was not working, but that is no longer the case.  Cash drawer is working as expected in 243.10.3.

Previous ticket: [https://jumpmind.atlassian.net/browse/JMCH-1023|https://jumpmind.atlassian.net/browse/JMCH-1023|smart-link] 

This is the relevant error:

{{java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: 'name' must not be null}}

h3. What’s happening

# *Request comes in*
{{PrintDocumentsEndpoint.printDocuments}} pulls {{printerId}} from the request.
{noformat}String printerId = request.getPrinterId();{noformat}
# *Printer opening logic*
Upon following the execution code, we can see the {{PrinterFactory.openPrinter()}} get invoked.  Because mobile printing is disabled, it calls:
{noformat}this.openPrinterFromType(printerId);{noformat}
But the method signature expects a *printer type*, not an ID.
# *Config lookup*
{{getPrinterConfig}} looks up configs under {{openpos.devices.printers.<printerType>}}.
Since it’s passed an *ID* ({{9788-p1}}), there’s no matching config → empty map.
{noformat}PrinterConfig config = this.getPrinterConfig(printerType); 
// returns object with settings as empty map because "9788-p1" isn’t a defined printerType{noformat}
# *Protocol resolution fails*
With no settings in the config, {{config.getSettings().get("protocol")}} returns {{null}}.
Then it calls:
{noformat}this.applicationContext.getBean(null, IPrinterProtocol.class);{noformat}
This causes the error that we see in the logs.



Ultimately, the issue occurs because {{this.openPrinterFromType(printerId)}} is getting the printer id, instead of the printer type.

h3. TVS Work-Around

I have created a TVS specific implementation for {{PrintDocumentsEndpoint}}.  In this implementation, we hook into the request and update the {{printerId}} to be the {{printerType}} because that is what {{PrinterFactory.openPrinterFromType}} is expecting. 

This work around has not been extensively tested.  It will be today and the rest of this week.  TVS would like this to be fixed in the base product.  I will have a ticket on their board to track this JMCH.  Once the fix has been provided, the below change will be reverted to ensure that TVS’s build is relying on base logic.

{noformat}package org.jumpmind.pos.document.service;

import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;
import org.jumpmind.pos.context.service.IContextService;
import org.jumpmind.pos.document.service.model.PrintDocumentResponse;
import org.jumpmind.pos.document.service.model.PrintDocumentsRequest;
import org.jumpmind.pos.document.service.model.ReceiptPrinter;
import org.jumpmind.pos.service.Endpoint;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Qualifier;

import static org.jumpmind.pos.util.RestApiSupport.REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH;

@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/document/print", implementation = "tvs-document")
@Slf4j
public class TvsPrintDocumentsEndpoint {

    private final IDocumentService documentService;
    private final PrintingHelper printingHelper;
    private final IContextService contextService;
    @Qualifier("printDocumentsEndpoint")
    private final PrintDocumentsEndpoint baseImpl;

    public TvsPrintDocumentsEndpoint(
            @Qualifier("printDocumentsEndpoint") PrintDocumentsEndpoint baseImpl,
            IDocumentService documentService,
            PrintingHelper printerHelper,
            IContextService contextService
    ) {
        this.baseImpl = baseImpl;
        this.documentService = documentService;
        this.printingHelper = printerHelper;
        this.contextService = contextService;
    }

    public PrintDocumentResponse printDocuments(PrintDocumentsRequest request) {
        if (!printingHelper.isMobilePrintingEnabled()) {
            updatePrinterIdToPrinterType(request);
        }
        return baseImpl.printDocuments(request);
    }

    private void updatePrinterIdToPrinterType(PrintDocumentsRequest request) {
        ReceiptPrinter printer = documentService.getDefaultPrinter().getPrinter();
        String to = null;
        if (printer != null) {
            to = printer.getPrinterType();
        } else {
            to = contextService.getString("openpos.devices.defaultPrinter", "HpPrinterSerial");
        }
        log.info("Updating PrintDocumentRequest.printerId from {} to {}", request.getPrinterId(), to);
        request.setPrinterId(to);
    }
}{noformat}



h3. Proposed Solutions

pass printer type from receipt printer table entry into {{openPrinterFromType}}

{noformat}    public IReceiptPrinter openPrinter(String printerId) throws PrintException {
        if (printingHelper.isMobilePrintingEnabled()) {
            return openMobilePrinter(printerId);
        } else {
            return openPrinterFromType(printerId);
        }
    }{noformat}



update {{printerType}} to {{printerId}} and use repostiory to pull printer object to get printerType

{noformat}    private IReceiptPrinter openPrinterFromType(String printerType) throws PrintException {
        if (printerType == null) {
            throw new PrintException("No openpos.defaultPrinter parameter defined.  Cannot lookup a default printer.");
        }

        PrinterConfig config = getPrinterConfig(printerType);
        String protocol = (String) config.getSettings().get("protocol");

        IPrinterProtocol printerProtocol = applicationContext.getBean(protocol, IPrinterProtocol.class);

        return tryOpen(printerType, config, printerProtocol);
    }{noformat}



