When {{openpos.devices.enableMobilePrint}} is enabled, the opposite happens.  The printer does work, but the cash drawer does not.  Since this configuration is deprecated and we have been advised to move away from it, I will not include details for this setup unless asked for.

This looks like a base issue and  involves use of quantities:

The {{RetailLineItem}} has two properties for tax: {{taxAmount}}, which is the total tax, and {{taxSaleLineItems}}, which is a list of all taxes.

For Returned Items, taxes are calculated in buildReceiptedReturnLineItem method in AddReturnItemToTransEndpoint.



And TaxAmount and TaxLines are calculated using the following method by determining the amount for a single item and then multiplying it by the quantity to be returned.

{noformat}public static Money adjustForQuantity(Money origAmount, BigDecimal origQuantity, BigDecimal currQuantity, BigDecimal availForReturn) {
    final Money proratedAmount;
    final Money origUnitAmount = origAmount.dividedBy(origQuantity, HALF_DOWN);

    if (isEqual(currQuantity, origQuantity)) {
        proratedAmount = origAmount;
    } else if (isEqual(availForReturn, currQuantity) || isEqual(origQuantity, currQuantity)) {
        final Money allButLast = origUnitAmount.multipliedBy(currQuantity.subtract(ONE), HALF_UP);
        final Money last = origAmount.minus(origUnitAmount.multipliedBy(origQuantity.subtract(ONE), HALF_UP));

        proratedAmount = allButLast.plus(last);
    } else {
        proratedAmount = origUnitAmount.multipliedBy(currQuantity, HALF_UP);
    }
    return proratedAmount;
}{noformat}

The return/sale screen sums the list of tax lines to calculate total tax, while the tender screen uses the already summed {{taxAmount}}. The discrepancy between these two leads to an amount not being returned as cash.

The rounding differences between {{taxAmount}} and the sum of individual tax line items cause this issue. Occasionally, both values match, resulting in correct calculations.

I have attached an Excel file demonstrating this. In one transaction, the amounts do not match, while in another, they do.

