Description:
TVS is seeing an issue where the customer display is not displaying the {{CustomerDisplayRDDealsMarketing}} screen (see attached image for screen that is no longer displaying). 



Technical analysis:

In {{RepeatDeliveryDealsState.onArrive()}}, the following method is invoked.

{{makeCustomerDisplayRequest("DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing", customerDisplayParams);}}

This instantiates an {{AppEvent}} with request type {{DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing}} and send it to paired customer display state manager.

Via debugging, I can confirm that the AppEvent is hitting {{CustomerDisplaySaleState.handleEvent()}}.

{noformat}@OnEvent(sources = EventSource.PARENT)
protected void handleEvent(AppEvent event) {
...
}{noformat}



However, this method does not appear to have any logic to handle the {{DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing}} request type, thus the {{DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing}} action is never executed to launch the customer display into {{CustomerDisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketingState}}.



This has been an issue we have seen before.  A JMCH was created [https://jumpmind.atlassian.net/browse/JMCH-392|https://jumpmind.atlassian.net/browse/JMCH-392|smart-link] .

The workaround we had was to create a event handler for {{EventSource.SELF}}.   At the time, when the customer display received an event from the parent, it would also send an event to itself.  Therefore the below code fixed the issue.

{noformat}import org.jumpmind.pos.util.event.*;

@State(name = "CustomerDisplaySaleState", appId = AppIdConstants.CUSTOMER_DISPLAY)
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class OnDisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketingEvent {

    private final ActionHelper actionHelper;

    @OnEvent(sources = EventSource.SELF)
    public void onHandleRepeatDeliveryConfirmationEvent(AppEvent event) {
        if (event instanceof RequestEvent<?> reqEvent && "DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing".equals(reqEvent.getRequest())) {
            actionHelper.doAction("DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing", ((RequestEvent<?>) event).getPayload());
        }
    }
}{noformat}



It appears that the customer display no longer sends events to itself. Below is from release notes for 243.6.  This _could_ be why we are not seeing the workaround working.  I’m not sure since TVS doesn’t know when this issue was reintroduced.

* _Technical | There are @Async operations (like event publishing) that create new threads on every operation. This can cause OOM error on thread creation (JMC-6337)_



A suggested solution is to add logic for handling {{AppEvent}} with request type {{DisplayRepeatDeliveryDealsMarketing}} in the implementation for {{CustomerDisplaySaleState.handleEvent()}}.

