Description:
*Summary*
Currently, the product does not support extending {{dml}} templates in the customer layer without losing the other {{dml}} definitions in {{sls-dml.yml}}. This creates inconsistency compared to {{sls-query.yml}}, where extending queries works seamlessly without overwriting other base query definitions.

*Details*

* In version *243.10.3*, when attempting to extend an existing {{dml}} (example below), all other {{dml}} definitions in {{sls-dml.yml}} are lost.
* As a result, POS cannot execute {{updateOriginalLineItem}} or {{updateOriginalLineItemPriceModifier}} since those do not exist in the customer-layer {{sls-dml.yml}}, resulting in a shrug.  

{noformat}---
dmls:
  - name: updateOrderItemsStatus
    dml: >
      update OrderLineItemModel
      set order_item_status_code = ${orderItemStatusCode},
          reason_code = case when ${reasonCode} <> '' then ${reasonCode} else reason_code end
    where: order_id = ${orderId}
    optionalWhereClauses:
      - line_sequence_number in (${lineSequenceNumbers})
{noformat}

*Comparison with Queries*

* Extending individual queries in {{sls-query.yml}} works as expected because the implementation of {{addQueries}} merges into the existing set of queries.
* However, the implementation of {{addDmls}} replaces the entire map instead of merging.

{noformat}public void addQueries(String deviceMode, List<QueryTemplate> queries) {
    Map<String, QueryTemplate> deviceModeTemplates = (Map)this.queriesByDeviceMode.getOrDefault(deviceMode, new HashMap());
    if (queries != null) {
        queries.forEach((it) -> deviceModeTemplates.put(it.getName(), it.copy()));
    }
    this.queriesByDeviceMode.put(deviceMode, deviceModeTemplates);
}

public void addDmls(String deviceMode, List<DmlTemplate> dmls) {
    this.dmlsByDeviceMode.put(deviceMode, this.buildDmlTemplatesByNameMap(dmls));
}
{noformat}

*Request*

* Update the implementation of {{addDmls}} to be consistent with {{addQueries}} by merging instead of replacing.
* This would allow customer-layer {{sls-dml.yml}} files to override or extend individual DMLs without losing the other base definitions.

*Benefit*

* Improves consistency between queries and DML behavior.
* Enables customers to extend or adjust individual DML templates without redefining the entire set.
* Reduces maintenance overhead and supports more flexible customer-layer customization.

*Priority*

* Not urgent, but would be a valuable *quality-of-life enhancement*.  There have been a handful of scenarios within TVS project that this would have been convenient.

