05/Feb/26 10:49 AM;712020:61efe601-852c-484a-b796-0d181e249f1d;h3. Yes, this is possible, but there is no built-in method currently exposed for it. Below are the available approaches:

h3. *Root Cause*

Each scan creates an action queued in {{StateManager.actionQueue}}. When the max quantity prompt appears, previously queued scans are still waiting. After dismissing the prompt, each queued scan triggers the condition again, causing multiple prompts.

----

h3. *Solution Options*

h4. *Option 1: Clear the Action Queue (Direct Answer)*

The {{StateManager}} has an internal {{actionQueue}} that can be cleared. While there is no public method currently exposed for this, you can access it as follows:

{noformat}@In(scope = ScopeType.Device)
private IStateManager stateManager;

@Override
public void handleItemAction(Action action, Item item, AppContext appContext, String bundleName) {
    // Clear queued actions before showing the prompt
    if (stateManager instanceof StateManager sm) {
        sm.actionQueue.clear();  // Clears ALL pending actions
    }

    // Show the prompt
    buildMaxQuantityPrompt(action, item, appContext, bundleName);
}
{noformat}

{quote}*Note:* This clears all pending actions, not just scans. If you need to clear only scan actions, we can add a {{drainActionsByName(String... actionNames)}} method to the framework.{quote}

----

h4. *Option 2: State Flag Pattern (Alternative - No Queue Clearing)*

If you prefer not to clear the queue, you can use a scope flag to prevent subsequent scans from triggering the prompt while it's active:

*In your action handler (set flag when showing prompt):*

{noformat}stateManager.setScopeValue(ScopeType.Conversation, "maxQuantityPromptActive", true);
{noformat}

*In your required action checker (skip if flag is set):*

{noformat}Boolean promptActive = stateManager.getScopeValue(ScopeType.Conversation, "maxQuantityPromptActive");
if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(promptActive)) {
    return Collections.emptyList();  // Don't add required actions
}
{noformat}

This approach lets queued scans process but prevents them from triggering the max quantity prompt again.

----

h3. *Recommendation*

* *Option 1* directly answers your question about clearing the queue, though the trade-off is that it clears all pending actions.
* *Option 2* is safer if you want to preserve other queued actions while still preventing duplicate prompts.

