h3. Description

TVS’s customer CRM integration relies on sending *only updated fields* to CRM. This is handled through the {{additionalFields}} map on the {{CustomerModel}}, which tracks field changes (e.g., {{"emailChanged": true}}).

When a customer is edited, the following logic determines which fields were updated:

{noformat}private void setUpdatedFieldGlobalVariables(CustomerModel jmcCustomer) {
    noYearBirthdayUpdated = hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "noYearBirthday");
    isPrimaryEmailUpdated = hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "email");
    isPrimaryEmailOptInStatusUpdated = hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "optIntoEmailMarketing");
    isPrimaryMailOptInStatusUpdated = hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "optIntoMailMarketing");
    isPrimaryPhoneUpdated = hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "phone");
    isPrimaryAddressUpdated =  hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(jmcCustomer, "address");
}

private boolean hasFormFieldBeenUpdated(CustomerModel jmcCustomer, String formFieldId) {
    return Boolean.TRUE.equals(jmcCustomer.getAdditionalFields().get(String.format("%sChanged", formFieldId)));
}{noformat}



In base, the method {{OnUpdateCustomer.madeChanges()}} is responsible for populating the {{additionalFields}} map with entries like {{"emailChanged": true}}, {{"firstNameChanged": true}}, etc., when customer information changes.



{noformat}    private boolean madeChanges(Form changedForm) {
        List<String> addressFields = this.contextClient.getList("openpos.customer.addressFormFields", String.class);
        Map<String, String> mapOfEnabledFields = (Map)this.initialCustomerEditForm.getFormElements().stream().map((field) -> {
            FormField formField = (FormField)field;
            if (StringUtils.isEmpty(formField.getValue())) {
                formField.setValue("");
            }

            return formField;
        }).filter((field) -> !field.isReadOnly()).collect(Collectors.toMap(FormField::getId, FormField::getValue));
        Stream var10000 = changedForm.getFormElements().stream();
        Objects.requireNonNull(FormField.class);
        List<FormField> changedFields = (List)var10000.map(FormField.class::cast).filter((field) -> {
            String previousValue = (String)mapOfEnabledFields.get(field.getId());
            if (field instanceof DatePartChooserField currentDatePart) {
                DatePartChooserField oldDatePart = (DatePartChooserField)this.initialCustomerEditForm.getFormElement(field.getId());
                return !currentDatePart.equalYearMonthDayValues(oldDatePart);
            } else if (field instanceof FormFieldWithList && this.i18nUtils.isKeyString(previousValue)) {
                return !this.i18nUtils.getStringOrDefault(previousValue, this.i18nClient.getLocaleAsString(LocaleType.DISPLAY)).equals(field.getValue());
            } else if (StringUtils.isEmpty(previousValue)) {
                return !field.isReadOnly() && !StringUtils.isEmpty(field.getValue());
            } else {
                return !field.isReadOnly() && !previousValue.equals(field.getValue());
            }
        }).peek((changedField) -> {
            if (addressFields.contains(changedField.getId())) {
                this.addressChanged = true;
                this.customer.setAdditionalField("addressChanged", true);
            }

            if (changedField.getFieldId().equalsIgnoreCase("contactmail")) {
                this.addressContactPrefChanged = true;
            }

            if (changedField.getFieldId().toLowerCase().contains("phone") || changedField.getFieldId().equalsIgnoreCase("contactsmstext")) {
                this.phoneChanged = true;
            }

            if (changedField.getFieldId().toLowerCase().contains("email")) {
                this.emailChanged = true;
            }

            this.customer.setAdditionalField(changedField.getId() + "Changed", true);
        }).collect(Collectors.toList());
        return !changedFields.isEmpty() || this.addressChanged;
    }{noformat}



h3. Expected Behavior

When editing customer information on *either the associate-facing display* or the *customer display*, the {{UpdateCustomer}} action handler should be invoked so that {{additionalFields}} is properly updated with the changed field indicators.



h3. Actual Behavior

* When editing a customer on the *associate-facing display*, {{UpdateCustomer}} is invoked and {{additionalFields}} is updated correctly.
* When editing a customer on the *customer display*, the application does *not* appear to hit the {{UpdateCustomer}} action handler.
** As a result, {{additionalFields}} is missing the key-value pairs (e.g., {{"emailChanged": true}}) required for CRM to identify which fields have changed.

This behavior is *not consistent* with version *243.7.2*, where the {{UpdateCustomer}} handler was invoked after edits on the customer display.



