h2. Root Cause Analysis

The duplicate payloads sent to downstream systems are caused by *missing publish suppression logic* in the transaction save flow. When database persistence failures occur during transaction processing (due to invalid UTF-8 byte sequences or JSON deserialization errors), the system:

# *First Publish*: Saves the transaction in an error state (ORPHANED/CANCELLED) and immediately publishes it via {{TransRepository.saveForPublishing()}}
# *Second Publish*: After recovery, saves the transaction again with final status (COMPLETED/CANCELLED) and publishes again

This results in duplicate payloads for the same transaction being sent to SAP and other downstream systems.

*Evidence:*

* {{TransRepository.save()}} (line 268-270) unconditionally calls {{saveForPublishing(transaction)}} regardless of transaction status
* {{FinalizeSaleSessionEndpoint.java}} (lines 180-195) catches RuntimeExceptions for ORPHANED/CANCELLED transactions and saves a "placeholder" transaction, which still triggers publishing
* No status-based filtering exists in {{saveForPublishing()}} method
* The {{IPublishService.publish()}} is called without checking if the transaction is in an error/incomplete state

