20/Jan/26 6:47 AM;712020:877ebe8a-e44a-419d-b0bd-b385e6a816f3;*Root Cause Analysis (Log / Code Based)*

The absence of the *Post Void* option for transactions that include a coupon is due to existing transaction evaluation logic, not a UI regression.

Based on the transaction flow and code path:

* The visibility of *Post Void* is controlled by {{isTransVoidable(TransactionSummary)}}.
* This method explicitly blocks Post Void when {{transactionSummary.isHasReturnedItems()}} is {{true}}.

{noformat}public boolean isTransVoidable(TransactionSummary transactionSummary) {
    if (!transactionSummary.isVoidable() || transactionSummary.isHasReturnedItems()) {
        return false;
    }
{noformat}

* The {{hasReturnedItems}} flag is derived from {{hasReturnedLineItem()}}:

{noformat}public boolean hasReturnedLineItem() {
    return this.getRetailLineItems()
        .stream()
        .filter(RetailLineItemModel::isItemReturnable)
        .anyMatch(lineItemModel ->
            lineItemModel.getQuantityAvailForReturn()
                .compareTo(lineItemModel.getQuantity()) < 0
        );
}
{noformat}

*Key Finding from Logs / Transaction Data*

* Coupon is added as a *RetailLineItem* with:
** {{quantity = 1}}
** {{quantityAvailForReturn = 0}}
** Non-returnable behavior
* This causes the condition {{0 < 1}} to evaluate to *true*, marking the transaction as having returned items.

*Resulting Behavior*

* {{hasReturnedItems = true}}
* {{isTransVoidable = false}}
* *Post Void is suppressed* on the View Details screen

*UI Consistency*

* Same behavior exists in *Old UI* and *New UI*.
* Old UI showed Post Void on the landing page but removed it on View Details after evaluation.
* New UI renders actions only after View Details, exposing the same logic earlier.

*Conclusion*
Transactions containing coupons are intentionally treated as non-voidable due to coupon line items being evaluated as returned items. This is expected behavior per current logic and not a regression in version *250.1.0*.

