09/Jan/26 3:38 PM;712020:0b3de8b9-fd84-40a7-a9ca-77e86f66a0b0; Investigation Complete

  I've successfully investigated Jira ticket JMCH-1422 and identified the root cause of the issue. Here's what I found:

  The Problem

  When using the new React UI (client-v2), the store close flow gets stuck after printing the store close report. The print completes successfully, but the POS doesn't proceed to the next step.

  Root Cause

  The new client (client-v2/projects/framework/printing/src/print-listener.service.ts:69-71) is missing critical logic to send a follow-up action after printing completes.

  Old client (working):
  // Sends PrintNextDocument action after successful print
  messageRegistry.sendMessage(r.message.src, new ActionMessage('PrintNextDocument', true))

  New client (broken):
  // Only logs, doesn't send any action!
  .subscribe(({ message, printRequest, err }) => {
      console.log({{Print response: ${message}}}, printRequest, err);
  });

  The Fix

  Update print-listener.service.ts to dispatch a ScreenAction with:

* Action name: 'PrintNextDocument' (on success) or 'PrintError' (on failure)
* doNotBlockForResponse: true

20/Jan/26 1:07 PM;712020:8b234d7e-962d-4107-8fb4-b2943c64dde2;h1. AI Investigation Summary

h2. Root Cause Analysis

The POS application becomes unresponsive after clicking 'Yes' on the 'Print Report' prompt during store close flow because the *new React UI (client-v2) is missing critical logic to send a follow-up action after printing completes*.

*The Problem:*

The server-side state machine ({{PrintStoreCloseReportState}}) expects a {{PrintNextDocument}} action to proceed after each print completes, but the client-v2 {{PrintListenerService}} never sends this action. The print completes successfully, but the state machine waits indefinitely for the response action.

*Evidence:*

