h2. Root Cause Analysis

The incorrect expected till amount ($434 instead of $300) on Device 014 was caused by *store-level till state synchronization inheriting unreconciled cash from a transaction with a missing session ID*.

*Evidence:*

* Transaction 2577 from Device 011 ($134.05 cash) had a *null session ID*, preventing it from being associated with Device 011's till session
* When Device 014 reopened on 2025-11-25 after 10 days of inactivity, the store-wide till synchronization logic (via {{OpsDataSyncListener}} processing {{ops_unit_status}} and {{ops_till}} at 20:43:01.650) calculated the opening balance
* The {{sessionSummaryBySessionId}} query in {{sls-query.yml}} filters by {{t.SESSION_ID = ${sessionId}}}, which *excludes transactions with null session IDs* from session totals
* However, the orphaned $134.05 was accumulated at the store level and incorrectly propagated to Device 014's {{expectedOpeningFloat}} during synchronization
* Device 014's till was last reconciled on 2025-11-24T19:55:19.909724 with business date 20251124, creating a 10-day gap

h2. Affected Components

* {{OpenTillEndpoint.java}}: {{headless/point-of-sale/ops/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/ops/service/OpenTillEndpoint.java}}
* {{OpsHelper.java}}: {{headless/point-of-sale/ops/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/ops/service/OpsHelper.java}}
* {{GetSessionTotalEndpoint.java}}: {{headless/point-of-sale/ops/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/ops/service/GetSessionTotalEndpoint.java}}
* {{sls-query.yml}}: {{headless/services/sales/src/main/resources/sls-query.yml}} (sessionSummaryBySessionId query)

h2. Recommended Fix

h3. Immediate Workaround (For JD Sports)

*Step 1: Correct the Till's Expected Opening Float*

Run the following SQL to reset Device 014's till to the correct configured float amount:

{code:sql}-- First, identify the affected till
SELECT till_id, business_unit_id, expected_opening_float, desired_float_amount, session_id, last_update_time
FROM ops_till
WHERE business_unit_id = '<STORE_ID>'
  AND till_id = '014';

-- Reset the expected opening float to the configured amount ($300)
UPDATE ops_till
SET expected_opening_float = 300.00,
    last_update_time = NOW(),
    last_update_by = 'SUPPORT_FIX'
WHERE business_unit_id = '<STORE_ID>'
  AND till_id = '014';{code}

*Step 2: Identify and Fix the Orphaned Transaction*

Find and assign the orphaned transaction to a reconciliation session:

{code:sql}-- Find transactions with null session IDs for this store
SELECT t.device_id, t.business_date, t.sequence_number, t.session_id, t.till_id,
       tli.tender_amount, tli.tender_type_code
FROM sls_trans t
JOIN sls_tender_line_item tli ON t.device_id = tli.device_id 
  AND t.business_date = tli.business_date 
  AND t.sequence_number = tli.sequence_number
WHERE t.business_unit_id = '<STORE_ID>'
  AND t.trans_status = 'COMPLETED'
  AND (t.session_id IS NULL OR t.session_id = '')
  AND tli.tender_type_code = 'CASH'
ORDER BY t.create_time DESC;

-- If transaction 2577 from Device 011 is found, assign it to a reconciliation session
-- or mark it as reconciled to prevent future propagation{code}

h3. Long-Term Code Fix (Option 3 - Recommended)

*Isolate Till Opening Float from Store-Level Cash*

Modify {{OpenTillEndpoint.java}} to detect stale till state and reset to configured float:

{code:java}// File: headless/point-of-sale/ops/src/main/java/org/jumpmind/pos/ops/service/OpenTillEndpoint.java
// Add this method to detect stale till state

private boolean isTillStateStale(TillModel till) {
    // Get the last till status to determine inactivity period
    UnitStatusModel lastStatus = opsRepository.findMostRecentTillStatus(
        till.getBusinessUnitId(), till.getTillId());

    if (lastStatus == null) {
        return true; // No status means new till, use configured float
    }

    LocalDateTime lastActivity = lastStatus.getRequestTime();
    if (lastActivity == null) {
        return true;
    }

    Duration inactivityPeriod = Duration.between(lastActivity, LocalDateTime.now());
