27/Jan/26 9:01 AM;712020:ad7b5cf3-9cd3-4ec8-a07c-c53367ad4328;h1. AI Investigation Summary

h2. Root Cause Analysis

The customer's expectation that setting {{order_eligible=0}} in {{itm_selling_rule}} would prevent Gift Cards from being sold in Order transactions is *incorrect based on how the code is designed*. The {{order_eligible}} flag works in the *opposite direction* - it's an *exception/override mechanism*, not a restriction mechanism.

*Evidence:*

* In {{AbstractAddItemToTransEndpoint.java}} (line 103), the critical logic is:

{code:java}if (config != null && !config.isSaleAllowed() && 
    !(item.getSellingRule().isOrderEligible() && 
      itemEntry.getLineItemTypeCode() == LineItemTypeCode.ORDER_IN_STORE)) {{code}

* This condition means: When {{order_eligible=1}} (true), items that would normally be blocked (e.g., {{isSaleAllowed()=false}}) *CAN* be sold in ORDER_IN_STORE transactions (it creates an exception)
* When {{order_eligible=0}} (false), items that would normally be blocked remain blocked, BUT items that are normally sellable ({{isSaleAllowed()=true}}) *remain sellable in ALL transaction types*
* The {{disableMixedBasket}} configuration only prevents mixing STORE_SALE items with ORDER_IN_STORE items in the same transaction - it does NOT prevent specific item types from being sold in Order transactions

*Key Finding*: The {{order_eligible}} flag does NOT restrict items from Order transactions - it only provides an exception to allow otherwise non-sellable items in Order transactions. This is a *product limitation*, not a defect.

h2. Affected Components

* {{AbstractAddItemToTransEndpoint.java}} - {{checkPerSellStatusCodeRules()}} method at line 103
* {{AddItemToTransEndpoint.java}} - {{disableMixedBasket}} logic at lines 43-51
* {{SellingRuleModel.java}} - {{orderEligible}} field definition at line 82

h2. Recommended Fix

*This requires a customer-layer customization* since base Commerce does not support restricting specific items from Order transactions based on the {{order_eligible}} flag.

h3. Option 1: Custom Endpoint Override (Recommended)

Create a custom endpoint that extends {{AddItemToTransEndpoint}} to add validation logic:

*Step 1: Create the custom endpoint class*

File: {{customer-layer/src/main/java/com/jdna/sales/service/trans/JdnaAddItemToTransEndpoint.java}}

{code:java}package com.jdna.sales.service.trans;

import org.jumpmind.pos.context.codes.LineItemTypeCode;
import org.jumpmind.pos.context.service.model.InputType;
import org.jumpmind.pos.item.service.model.FindItemResponse;
import org.jumpmind.pos.item.service.model.Item;
import org.jumpmind.pos.sales.service.trans.AddItemToTransEndpoint;
import org.jumpmind.pos.sales.service.trans.model.AddItemToTransRejectionTypeCode;
import org.jumpmind.pos.sales.service.trans.model.AddItemToTransRequest;
import org.jumpmind.pos.sales.service.trans.model.AddItemToTransResponse;
import org.jumpmind.pos.service.Endpoint;
import lombok.extern.slf4j.Slf4j;

import static org.jumpmind.pos.util.RestApiSupport.REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH;

@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/transmgmt/items/add", implementation = "jdna")
@Slf4j
public class JdnaAddItemToTransEndpoint extends AddItemToTransEndpoint {

    @Override
    public AddItemToTransResponse addItemToTransaction(AddItemToTransRequest request) {
        // Check if this is an ORDER_IN_STORE transaction
        if (request.getItemEntry() != null && 
            request.getItemEntry().getLineItemTypeCode() != null &&
            request.getItemEntry().getLineItemTypeCode().isNewOrderWithDelivery()) {

            InputType inputType = getInputType(request.getItemEntry());
            String businessDate = null;
            if (contextService.getBoolean("openpos.promotions.useBusinessDateAsEffectiveDate", false)) {
                businessDate = request.getBusinessDate();
            }

            FindItemResponse itemResponse = searchItem(
                inputType, 
                request.getItemEntry(), 
                null, 
                businessDate
            );

            if (itemResponse.isItemFound()) {
                Item item = itemResponse.getItem();
                // Check if order_eligible is false (0) - RESTRICT from orders
                if (item.getSellingRule() != null && 
                    !item.getSellingRule().isOrderEligible()) {
                    log.info("Item {} rejected from Order transaction - order_eligible=false", 
                        item.getItem().getItemId());
                    return new AddItemToTransResponse(
                        AddItemToTransRejectionTypeCode.ITEM_NOT_SELLABLE,
                        item.getItem().getItemId()
                    );
                }
            }
        }

        // Continue with standard processing
        return super.addItemToTransaction(request);
    }
}{code}

