h2. Root Cause Analysis

The New UI's {{NavigationCardGroupCardsComponent}} template only renders the {{icon}} field from {{ActionItem}}, which is designed for icon font names (like Material Icons). It does not support the {{imageUrl}} field for custom images.

*Root Cause Chain:*

# {{ctx_button.icon_type}} database column contains image URLs/paths for some tiles (e.g., {{content:report-icon}}, {{/images/talent.png}})
# {{ActionHelper.getActionItem()}} copies {{icon_type}} directly to {{ActionItem.icon}} field (line 68-73)
# {{NavigationCardGroupCardsComponent}} template renders {{{{ card.action.icon }}}} which outputs the URL as text inside {{<jme-icon>}} component
# The {{<jme-icon>}} component expects icon font names, not URLs, so it fails to render images

*Evidence:*

* {{navigation-card-group-cards.component.html}} line 8: {{<jme-icon>{{ card.action.icon }}</jme-icon>}} - only uses icon field
* {{ActionItem.java}} has both {{icon}} (line 48) and {{imageUrl}} (line 49) fields, but {{imageUrl}} is never populated by {{ActionHelper}}
* {{ActionHelper.java}} line 68-73: {{.icon(model.getIconType())}} - always sets icon, never imageUrl
* {{ButtonModel.java}} line 52: {{iconType}} is a String field that can contain either icon names OR image URLs

