The {{TransMgmtClient:recordGiftCardItem}} makes a series of calls when adding a gift card item - it calls {{transMgmtService.recordGiftCardAction}} to record the action and add the GC item to the transaction.  If the call is successful, the recordGiftCardItem method then updates the line item description using the below code block:

{noformat}String defaultItemDesc = response.getRetailLineItem().getItemDescription();
String translatedActionCode = i18nClient.getString(LocaleType.BUSINESS_UNIT, "giftcard", "giftcard.actionType." + defaultItemDesc.split(" - ")[1].toLowerCase());
response.getRetailLineItem().setItemDescription(defaultItemDesc.split(" - ")[0] + " - " + translatedActionCode);{noformat}

Petco has GC item descriptions that look like “GIFT CARD - NON DENOMINATION” which produces a {{translatedActionCode}} value of {{GIFT CARD - <MISSING RESOURCE key='giftcard.actionType.non denomination'>}} which is then set as the item’s description.

The logic used here to map the action type to an i18n key by assuming the number of dashes in a description is not good logic, and it is not reasonable to ask retailers to change their item data as item data may come from external integration or ingestion processes.  This can be fixed in an endpoint override, though this is ultimately a core bug as core is assuming/expecting item descriptions for gift cards specifically to follow a non-standard description pattern.

!Screenshot 2026-02-17 at 12.14.17 PM.png|width=926,height=105,alt="Screenshot 2026-02-17 at 12.14.17 PM.png"!

*Expectation:* The logic should be smarter about interpolating the description and attempting to affix the Gift Card action to the description.  It should be possible for “GIFT CARD - NON DENOMINATION - Issue” to be a line item description for gift cards, as retailers may have various types of gift cards that they’d like to present via dashes.

