*From:* John Varcho <jira@jumpmind.atlassian.net> 
*Sent:* Tuesday, March 3, 2026 8:18 AM
*To:* Rajbhandari, Yudeep <yudeep.rajbhandari@accenture.com>
*Subject:* [External] [JMCH-1714] Scanning gift card causes action to trigger more than once 

| |{color:#172b4d}*WARNING:*{color} {color:#172b4d}External email. Be vigilant with links, attachments, and requests.{color}| | |

{color:#999999}—-—-—-—{color}    

{color:#999999}Reply above this line.{color}   

{color:#333333}John Varcho commented:{color} 

h2. []{color:#333333}Analysis of 250.1.8 Logs (commerce-fixed (99) (1).log from 2026-02-27){color}

{color:#333333}*Key Findings:*{color} 

#   {color:#333333}*Version Confirmed:*{color}{color:#333333} Running 250.1.8 with the fix{color}
#   {color:#333333}*No "AcquiredCardData" action found:*{color}{color:#333333} Unlike the original ticket description which showed the AcquiredCardData transition, this log shows a  {color}{color:#333333}*different pattern*{color}{color:#333333} - multiple rapid-fire CheckForCardData actions being sent from the scanner{color}
#   {color:#333333}*Scanner Configuration:*{color} 
#*  {color:#333333}WedgeScanner enabled: startSequence=*, endSequence=Enter, enabled=true{color}
#*  {color:#333333}This indicates wedge scanner is sending data with prefix/suffix{color} 
#   {color:#333333}*The Issue Pattern:*{color} 
#*  {color:#333333}Scanner sends  CheckForCardData action with type=Dialog and doNotBlockForResponse=false{color}
#*  {color:#333333}The system properly processes the first one, but  {color}{color:#333333}*additional CheckForCardData actions continue to arrive*{color}
#*  {color:#333333}These subsequent actions arrive while already in a different state (e.g., ActivateGiftCardState, BbwGetGiftCardBalanceState, PostTenderAuthorizeGiftCardState){color}
#*  {color:#333333}Result: "Unexpected action 'CheckForCardData'" warnings because those states don't have handlers for that action{color} 



{color:#333333}*Example sequence from line 36647-36678:*{color} 

{noformat}14:01:39.235 - CheckForCardData received (while in BbwScanGiftCardState){noformat}

{noformat}14:01:39.302 - WARN: Unexpected action "CheckForCardData" (now in BbwGetGiftCardBalanceState){noformat}

{noformat}14:01:39.498 - CheckForCardData received AGAIN{noformat}

{noformat}14:01:39.539 - WARN: Unexpected action "CheckForCardData" (still in BbwGetGiftCardBalanceState){noformat}

{color:#333333}*Configuration Overrides Present:*{color} 

*  {color:#333333}Line 370: bbw-giftcard-flow-ext.yml loaded{color}
*  {color:#333333}Line 376: Overriding transition CancelActivation on state ScanGiftCardState{color}
*  {color:#333333}Line 500: Overriding original state: ScanGiftCardState with new state: BbwScanGiftCardState{color}



{color:#333333}*Assessment:*{color}{color:#333333}This appears to be a  {color}{color:#333333}*scanner/input configuration issue*{color}{color:#333333}, not a core state management defect after 250.1.8. The wedge scanner is sending multiple scan events for a single scan action.{color}   

