Description:
This issue was reported by TVS.  They are using Commerce version {{24.1.5-TVS}}.

If a customer opens the LinkedCustomerDetails screen on the customer display and doesn’t close it out, the screen stays on the customer display.  If the transaction is voided or completed, the LinkedCustomerDetails screen with the previous customer’s information still remains on the customer display.

Upon investigation, the following method gets ran after the transaction has been voided or completed.

{noformat}protected void cleanUpCustomerDisplaySession() {
    ...
    makeCustomerDisplayRequest("Cancel", null);
    ...
}{noformat}



The logs show that the {{Cancel}} action does get sent to the customer display, but it doesn’t do anything if the customer display is on the {{CustomerDisplayLinkedCustomerDetailsState}}.

Adding the following action handler to {{tvs-customer-display-flow-ext.yml}} resolves this issue.

{noformat}CustomerDisplayLinkedCustomerFlow:
  - CustomerDisplayLinkedCustomerDetailsState:
      Cancel: CompleteState{noformat}

