Description:
TVS has reported an issue where the gift card balance from an activation is not being printed on the sale receipt. I've attached the TVS receipt for reference.

In the base (customer/tvs/24.1), the following line from {{sale-receipt-body.md}} is responsible for displaying the balance of the gift card:

{noformat}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Balance:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${model.formatMoney(authLine.remainingBalanceAmount)}{noformat}

It appears that {{remainingBalanceAmount}} does not get set for the Authorization object in the Aurus implementation for activating a gift card. Below is the code responsible for mapping the Aurus response to JMC’s Authorization object:

{noformat}protected void processAuthorization(ActivateCardRequest request, ActivateCardResponse response, AurusTransDetailDatum transDetails) {
    Authorization authorization = getOrCreateAuthorization(response.getAuthorization());
    authorization.setResultCode(PaymentResultCode.OK);
    authorization.setRequestedAmount(request.getRequestedAmount());
    CurrencyUnit currencyUnit = request.getRequestedAmount().getCurrencyUnit();
    Money approvedAmount = Money.of(currencyUnit, Double.parseDouble(transDetails.getTransactionAmount()));
    authorization.setAuthorizedAmount(approvedAmount);
    authorization.setAuthTypeCode(AuthTypeCode.ACTIVATE);
    authorization.setPartiallyApproved(isPartiallyApproved(transDetails));
    authorization.setIsoCurrencyCode(currencyUnit.getCode());
    authorization.setAuthCode(transDetails.getApprovalCode());

    parseAuthMethodTypeCode(request.getCardDetailsInfo(), authorization);

    response.setAuthorization(authorization);
}{noformat}



To resolve this, I added the following setter and applied a patch to our lab. This change ensures the receipt prints the balance:

{noformat}authorization.setRemainingBalanceAmount(Money.of(currencyUnit, Double.parseDouble(transDetails.getBalanceAmount())));{noformat}

