Description:
*Reported build:*

This was reported on a build using {{commerceVersion=241.0.16}}.

*Reproduction Steps*

# Set the following config to true… {{openpos.documents.allowPrintingDependingOnLogic}}
# Start a transaction, add any item, and complete by tendering.
# On the receipt options screen, click ‘Email Receipt’.

BUG: Application hangs at loading screen.



Upon stepping through {{GenerateDocumentsState}}, it appears that the application doesn’t execute any actions, causing it to hang.

*Technical Notes*

After stepping through, here is what I found…

Once the the associate enters an email and continues, {{emailReceipt(String emailAddress)}} gets called.

{noformat}@ActionHandler
public void emailReceipt(String emailAddress) {
    emailForReceipt = emailAddress;

    if (isLinkedLoyaltyCustomerTransaction() && !emailAddress.equalsIgnoreCase(getSavedCustomerEmail())) {
        showSaveCustomerEmailPrompt();
    } else if (isEmailVerificationEnabled()) {
        promptForEmailVerify();
    } else {
        verifyEmailAccepted();
    }
}{noformat}

Code in the else block is executed.  {{verifyEmailAccepted()}} is called.

{noformat}public void verifyEmailAccepted() {
    queueEmailReceipt();

    if (!isPrintAndEmail && isConditionalPrintingEnabled()) {
        printReceipt(false);
    } else if (isPrintAndEmail) {
        printReceipt(true);
    } else if (!receiptsPrinted) {
        doAction("GenerateDocumentsFinish");
    }
}{noformat}

The email is successfully queued via {{queueEmailReceipt()}} and the code in the first condition block is executed.  {{printReceipt(false)}} is called.

{noformat}private void printReceipt(final boolean printCustomerCopy) {
    if (printCustomerCopy && isPromptForGiftReceiptCountRequired()) {
        showGiftReceiptCountPrompt();
    } else {
        printReceiptImpl(printCustomerCopy);
    }
}{noformat}

The code in the else block is executed.  {{printReceiptImpl(false)}} is called.

While in this method, a {{return}} is executed.

{noformat}if (documents == null || documents.isEmpty()) {
    log.info("No documents generated for trans {}", transaction);
    return;
}{noformat}



