Description:
TVS reported an issue with a specific transaction payload where  {{trans_status}} == {{"SUSPENDED"}} and {{trans_status_code}} *:* {{"ORPHANED"}}. This was a transaction that was resumed and then failed to attach the customer from the original transaction due to being unable to connect to CRM.  Please see below.

I believe this was reported on {{241.0.15}}.

h3. Root Cause:

A {{NullPointerException}} was encountered in the {{LoyaltyRewardsState}} due to the following issue:

{{Caused by: java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "org.jumpmind.pos.customer.model.CustomerModel.getAdditionalFields()" because the return value of "org.jumpmind.pos.sales.model.RetailTransModel.getCustomer()" is null}}

This issue occurred when transaction #6952 was resumed on device 0181-001. The original transaction had an attached customer, but upon resumption, a call to the CRM service failed, leading to the following error:

{{org.springframework.web.client.ResourceAccessException: I/O error on GET request for "https://crm-wrapper-int.vitaminshoppe.com/crm-service/customer/search": No route to host: no further information}}

As a result, {{appContext.getCurrentTransaction().getCustomer()}} returned null, causing an exception on this line in {{LoyaltyRewardsState}}:

{{Map<String, Object> additionalCustomerFields = appContext.getCurrentTransaction() == null ? null : appContext.getCurrentTransaction().getCustomer().getAdditionalFields();}}

h3. Application Behavior:

The application presumes that a customer is attached because the {{CheckForLoyaltyRewardsState}} includes logic to verify if there is a {{loyaltyCardNumber}} present in the transaction:

{noformat}public class CheckForLoyaltyRewardsState extends AbstractState {

    @OnArrive
    public void checkForLoyaltyRewards(Action action){
        if(appContext.getContextClient().is("openpos.sell.promptForLoyaltyRewardsFirst", true)
                && appContext.getCurrentTransaction().getLoyaltyCardNumber() != null){
            doAction("DoLoyaltyRewards");
        } else {
            doAction("Next");
        }
    }{noformat}

 

In this case, the {{loyaltyCardNumber}} was not null, as it was set in the original transaction. The application flow does not require a CRM call to maintain this value in the resumed transaction.

h3. Steps to Reproduce Locally:

# Start a transaction.
# Add an item.
# Attach a customer.
# Suspend the transaction.
# Resume the transaction. Force {{SearchCustomerEndpoint}} to not return a customer OR set {{appContext.getCurrentTransaction().setCustomer(null)}}
# Click checkout.

