This is an issue that is occurring with the TVS project (243.0.4) and is reproduceable with just the base project (branch releases/243.0). 

When navigating to the product details screen, a call is made to check the buddy store inventory. With the current hardcoded implementation, this call is immediate, and a table of stores with inventory counts appears in the Inventory section of the INFO tab.

However, when integrating the OMS service API, there is a delay of approximately 5-10 seconds to retrieve a response. Due to this delay, the buddy store table does not get populated in the INFO tab initially. The data only becomes visible if the user switches tabs or hits a media breakpoint.

*Steps to Reproduce*:

# Add the following 5 second timer to {{GetBuddyStoreEndpoint.getBuddyStores()}}:
{noformat}    long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
    long elapsedTime = 0L;

    while (elapsedTime < 5000) {
        //perform db poll/check
        elapsedTime = (new Date()).getTime() - startTime;
    }{noformat}
# Navigate to the product details screen for any product.
# Observe that the buddy store table is missing in the INFO tab.
# Switch to a different tab or hit a media breakpoint.
# Return to the INFO tab and observe that the buddy store table data is now visible.

