Description:
Ever since TVS upgraded to 243.3.0, we have been running into multiple issues with events between customer displays.  We’ve had to add {{@OnEvent}} annotated methods to essentially trigger an action on the customer display.

Below is example of this:

*REPRODUCTION STEPS:*

# Start transaction with customer display paired
# Attach customer
# Add Repeat Delivery Item
# Click Checkout
# Opt in for repeat delivery and continue

*BUG*: POS displays prompt indicating to the associate that the application is waiting for a confirmation from a customer on the customer display (pos_repeat_delivery_confirmation_pending.png)

*SOLUTION*:

{noformat}@State(name = "CustomerDisplaySaleState", appId = AppIdConstants.CUSTOMER_DISPLAY)
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class OnHandleRepeatDeliveryConfirmationEvent {

    private final ActionHelper actionHelper;

    @OnEvent(sources = EventSource.PARENT)
    public void onHandleRepeatDeliveryConfirmationEvent(AppEvent event) {
        if (event instanceof RequestEvent<?> reqEvent && "DisplayRepeatDeliveryConfirmation".equals(reqEvent.getRequest())) {
            actionHelper.doAction("DisplayRepeatDeliveryConfirmation", ((RequestEvent<?>) event).getPayload());
        }
    }
}{noformat}



We’ve needed to create other {{@OnEvent}} annotated methods since the upgrade too.  For now, we will check in the above change, but I wanted to 1) let JM know we are seeing this issue and 2) confirm if a change will be coming.  If a change is coming, I’m thinking we will want to revert these changes we have been making in the customer layer so that we are leveraging base.

