Description:
The following is listed as an anti-pattern {{MicroserviceEndpoints.md}}.

{noformat}## Anti-patterns - Developers should avoid subclassing an endpoint and relying on protected methods to change functionality.{noformat}

 

In the TVS project, we are setting a value on a custom field that we created for {{RetailLineItemModel}}.

{noformat}@Slf4j
@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/transmgmt/items/addReturn", implementation = "tvs-sales")
public class TvsAddReturnItemToTransEndpoint extends AddReturnItemToTransEndpoint {

    @Override
    public AddItemToTransResponse addReturnItemToTransaction(AddReturnItemToTransRequest request) {
        AddItemToTransResponse response = super.addReturnItemToTransaction(request);

        RetailLineItemModel lineItem = response.getSaleSession().getActiveTransaction().findRetailLineItem(response.getAddedLineNumber());
        if (lineItem != null) {
            this.setUpcOnRetailLineItemModelExtension(lineItem, request.getItemEntry());
        }

        return response;
    }{noformat}

 

We still want to use the base logic to add the actual return item.  But the docs tell us that we should avoid subclassing.  However, in this example, we still want to leverage the base code to add a return item.  The only reason we are creating our own implementation of this endpoint is to set a custom field.

The only way that I know that will allow us to leverage the base endpoint implementation still is by injecting a instance of that endpoint and then calling the exposed method that way.

{noformat}@Slf4j
@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/transmgmt/items/addReturn", implementation = "tvs-sales")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class TvsAddReturnItemToTransEndpoint {

    private final AddReturnItemToTransEndpoint baseEndpointImpl;
    private final IItemService itemService;

    public AddItemToTransResponse addReturnItemToTransaction(AddReturnItemToTransRequest request) {
        AddItemToTransResponse response = baseEndpointImpl.addReturnItemToTransaction(request);

        if (response.getSaleSession() != null) {
            RetailTransModel trans = response.getSaleSession().getActiveTransaction();
            if (trans != null) {
                RetailLineItemModel lineItem = trans.findRetailLineItem(response.getAddedLineNumber());
                if (lineItem != null) {
                    this.setUpcOnRetailLineItemModelExtension(lineItem, request.getItemEntry());
                }
            }
        }
        return response;
    }{noformat}

 

Below are the questions that this has brought up.

# Does this follow JM recommendations for extending endpoints?
# Pradeep asked this when going through the PR: Is there a reason why we shouldn’t be subclassing endpoints using base endpoints?

