Description:
*Background:* TVS requires the ability for the Point of Sale (POS) system to process returns as receipted returns, even if the original transaction exceeds their configured 30-day threshold defined in their return policy.

*Current Behavior:* Currently, when a transaction is older than 30 days, the system prompts the associate with the option to continue the return as non-receipted. The existing configuration ({{openpos.returns.rejectionOverridesAllowed.tooOld}}) is not functioning as intended due to an {{if}} condition in {{ItemReturnRejectedState.java}} that prevents it from being triggered.



*Proposed Change:*

# *New Option:* When scanning a receipt or product purchased over 30 days ago, add a new "Bypass" option to the pop-up that allows the return to proceed as a receipted return.
# *Permissions:* If this bypass button is clicked, then the POS should request manager override.



*Technical Details:*

* *Code Reference:*
** In {{ItemReturnRejectedState.java}}, the current check prevents the configuration from allowing the receipted return flow. The relevant section of code is:
* {noformat}if (rejectionCode.equals(ReturnRejectionCodes.QTY_NOT_AVAILABLE) || rejectionCode.equals(ReturnRejectionCodes.TOO_OLD)) {
    ActionItem continueNonReceipted = new ActionItem("ContinueWithNonReceipted", resource("message.return.item.button.continue.nonreceipted"));
    continueNonReceipted.setKeybind("Escape");
    buttons.add(continueNonReceipted);
} else if(returnsMgmtClient.returnOverrideAllowedOnProposedReturnPolicy()) {
    ActionItem continueOverride = new ActionItem("ContinueWithOverride", resource("message.return.item.button.continue.override"));
    continueOverride.setKeybind("Escape");
    buttons.add(continueOverride);
}
{noformat}
** The first {{if}} condition should be modified to allow for the new "Bypass" option when the transaction is too old but should still support existing logic.

*Acceptance Criteria:*

* When a receipt older than 30 days is scanned, a pop-up should display:
** Option to "Continue as Receipted Return" (Bypass)
** Option to "Cancel"
* The "Bypass" option should require manager level permission



*Official Requirement:*

When scanning a receipt or product that was purchased 31 days ago, the current pop-up places it as either continue as receipted return or cancel. They would like a “bypass” option where it would allow a receipted return flow to continue. They would also like this button to manager level permission.

