h3. Issue Summary:

Prior to the 243 upgrade, TVS was successfully printing chits for return items (see attached image). These chits were generated based on a document definition found in {{non-sell-item-receipt.yml}}. The chits were associated with {{commerceVersion 241.0.21}}.

However, after the upgrade to 243, TVS lost this functionality. It appears that the loss of this feature may be an unintended consequence of refactoring the base {{SaleState}} to use the new state pattern.

h3. Detailed Investigation:

In version 241, the following code snippet in {{SaleState.java}} is responsible for triggering the printing of non-sellable return item receipts:

{noformat}@ActionHandler
void onGenerateDocumentsFinish(Action action) {
    if (appContext.getCurrentTransaction().hasReturnLineItem()) {
        doAction("NonSellableReturnItems");
    } else {
        transactionFinished();
    }
}{noformat}

In this version, the action {{NonSellableReturnItems}} initiates the {{HandleNonSellableReturnItemsFlow}}, which is the flow that results in the printing of the {{non-sell-item-receipt}}.

h3. Findings in Version 243:

* I have reviewed the 243 upgrade and observed that the necessary YAML configurations, state definitions, and receipt templates are still present.
* However, I did not find any reference to the {{NonSellableReturnItems}} action being triggered in base version 243.
* Additionally, the {{onGenerateDocumentsFinish}} action handler is no longer present in {{SaleState.java}}.

Because the yaml configurations, state definitions, and receipt templates still exist in the base product, I believe that the removal of the functionality was not intentional (therefore a bug)

h3. Conclusion:

It seems that the 243 upgrade inadvertently removed or failed to include the necessary logic for launching the flow that ends up printing the non-sell-item-receipt.

h3. Request:

Please re-implement the {{NonSellableReturnItems}} action to ensure the chits for return items are printed as they were in version 241

