Description:
*Description of Issue:* when GC issue/load by card tender is Canceled. instead of screening back to “select tender options” screen, the payment is completed with the GC card in the transaction.

We don’t seem to be cleaning up cardDetails properly after a gift card activation, causing GetCardDataState to use the activated card for tender after a cancel

{noformat}@InOut(scope = ScopeType.Conversation, required = false)
protected CardDetailsInfo cardDetails;{noformat}

{noformat}} else if (cancelled.get() && this.cardDetails != null) {
    // If the cardDetails are not null, then they would have been provided by manual entry at the POS
    // (e.g., for gift cards) while a pending GCD request to the PINPad was simultaneously cancelled
    doAction("GetCardDataSuccess");{noformat}

The above code is from 243.0. It looks like this will be less likely to happen in 243.6, but could still happen if the gift card activation is keyed:

{noformat}} else if (cancelled.get() && this.cardDetails != null) {
    // If the cardDetails are not null, then they would have been provided by manual entry at the POS
