This bug was identified on {{commerceVersion=243.4.3}}.

Currently, TVS has the "order history" tab disabled on the linked customer details screen:

{noformat}openpos:
  customer:
    membership:
      orderHistoryTab:
        enabled: false{noformat}



Because of this:

When the method {{AbstractBuildLinkedCustomerDetailScreen.loadOrderHistory()}} is called, the method {{linkedCustomerDetailsOrderHistoryDataProvider.loadCustomerOrders()}} is not executed because the order history tab is disabled.

{noformat}protected void loadOrderHistory() {
    if (linkedCustomerDetailsScreenHelper.isOrderHistoryTabEnabled() && appContext.getLinkedCustomer() != null) {
        linkedCustomerDetailsOrderHistoryDataProvider.loadCustomerOrders(orderHistoryFilterOptions);
    }
}{noformat}



This is significant because {{loadCustomerOrders()}} is responsible for initializing {{orderHistory}} to an empty list:

{noformat}public void loadCustomerOrders(FilterOptions filter) {
    ...
    orderHistory = new ArrayList<>();
    ...{noformat}



Regardless of whether the tab is enabled, {{LinkedCustomerDetailsOrderHistoryDataProvider.getNextDataChunk()}} is still called:

{noformat}    @Override
    public List<UIOrderHistoryOrder> getNextDataChunk() {
        int startFrom = sentChunk * PAGE_SIZE;
        if (startFrom >= orderHistory.size()) {
            return new ArrayList<>();
        } else {
            sentChunk++;
            return orderHistory.stream().skip(startFrom).limit(PAGE_SIZE).map(this::toUIOrderHistoryOrder).toList();
        }{noformat}



However, since {{loadCustomerOrders()}} was never triggered (due to the tab being disabled), the {{orderHistory}} list remains uninitialized, which leads to a {{NullPointerException}} when attempting to access {{orderHistory.size()}}.

Error in logs:

{noformat}2024-12-05 10:22:35.194 ERROR [9780-001:20241122:24] [SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor-31] [SimpleAsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler] Unexpected exception occurred invoking async method: public void org.jumpmind.pos.core.service.UIDataMessageProviderService.updateProviders(org.jumpmind.pos.core.flow.ApplicationState,java.util.Map) 
