Description:
TVS reported the following issue:
While forced to change the password after its expiration, user is allowed to use the old password with contrast to when the user manually changes the password. The validators responsible for validating the old password in case of password expiration are not being called in this flow.

Here are the configuration of the validators:

{noformat}openpos:
  user:
    authentication:
      passwordValidation:
        - validationType: RequireMinLength
          validation: 7
        - validationType: RequireMaxLength
          validation: 8
        - validationType: ProhibitPrevious
          validation: 3{noformat}

Process to reproduce:

# As a prerequisite, update the EXPIRATION_TIME column in USR_PASSWORD_HISTORY to an already past timestamp for a particular user.
# Login in to the same user in POS, the password expiration prompt appears. Select ‘Yes’ to change password
# Enter the old password and the new passwords same as the older one
# Click ‘OK’
# It validates the older password as well.
# Required behaviour: It should not validate previously used passwords as configured in the  passwordValidation configuration, and display the password invalidation prompt. We need all validators to be enforced for password reset during the password expiration flow.


Investigated issue:
## Manual password change uses the following method in *ChangePasswordActionHandler* class to validate the user input password which correctly validates the password based on the configuration:

{noformat}private void changePassword(String oldPassword, String newPassword1, String newPassword2) {
    ...
    boolean newPasswordValid = this.userMgmtClient.isPasswordValid(newPassword1, this.currentUser);
    if (result.isValid() && newPasswordValid) {...}{noformat}
b. Password change via expiration uses the following method in *UserLoginManager* class to validate the password which does not include the validations configures on the configuration as displayed above:
{noformat}public void setNewPassword(Map<String, String> passwordData) {
    String oldPassword = (String)passwordData.get("oldpassword");
    String newPassword1 = (String)passwordData.get("newpassword1");
    String newPassword2 = (String)passwordData.get("newpassword2");
    AuthenticationRequest oldPasswordAuthenticationRequest = new AuthenticationRequest(this.enteredUserName, oldPassword.getBytes());
    UserModel user = this.userStrategy.validateUser(oldPasswordAuthenticationRequest).getUserModel();
    ValidatePasswordResult result = this.validateOldPasswordStrategy.validatePassword(oldPasswordAuthenticationRequest, user);
     if (!result.isValid()) {...}{noformat}


This issue is reported on{{commerceVersion=243.4.3}}

