Description:
TVS Reported the following issue:

When going through the repeat delivery scenario in ADP flow, Shipping address is not retrieved from the CRM given that billing address/primary address is incomplete, but the shipping address is correct.


Steps to reproduce:

# In JMC POS, link a customer whose primary billing address is incomplete but has a valid shipping Address as such:

{noformat}"addresses": [
        {
            "primary": true,
            "id": "1",
            "addressType": "HOME",
            "addressLine1": null,
            "addressLine2": null,
            "city": "****",
            "state": "****",
            "postalcode": "10001",
            "country": "USA",
            "mailOptIn": "Unknown",
            "modifiedDate": "2025-01-20"
        },
        {
            "primary": false,
            "id": "2",
            "addressType": "SHIP",
            "addressLine1": "123 3rd St",
            "addressLine2": null,
            "city": "****",
            "state": "****",
            "postalcode": "12302",
            "country": "USA",
            "mailOptIn": "Unknown",
            "modifiedDate": "2025-01-20"
        }
    ],{noformat}
# Add an Auto-Delivery eligible item to the transaction
#  Opt in for the ADP workflow with new billing address and shipping address in JMC. The billing address is not updated in CRM but the shipping address in updated in CRM
# Conclude the transaction
# Start a new ADP transaction with the same customer as previous.
# Sign-up for repeat delivery and the billing address form is displayed, populate the billing address (make sure Use as Shipping address checkbox is unchecked)
# Click Next and the shipping address form is displayed, instead of retrieving the previously set shipping address from the CRM, it opts in to add a new shipping address (screenshot provided).

Expected scenario: Shipping address should be fetched from the CRM and shown up as the option as provided in screenshot attached.

Investigated Issue:
While showing up the customer address screen, it runs through a validation of customer address which decides whether to display the “Enter address” form or the  ValidateAddress screen, as shown in the appContext.getOrderMgmtClient().validateCustomerForOrder(customer) function in showCustomerAddress() method in {{ChooseAddressState}}

{noformat}@OnArrive
    protected void showCustomerAddress() {
        this.workingAddress = this.getWorkingAddress();
        boolean autoPickAddress = this.appContext.getContextClient().is("openpos.orders.autoPickAddress", true);
