17/Oct/25 2:53 PM;62e96878d49df231b6276c30;Sure — here’s my understanding.

I believe this behavior is primarily tied to how TVS configured their employee discount promotion in Promote. The dataset referenced in the description should include the promotion data (Promotion ID: *PERMANENTPROMOS-3-1*).

In *prm-qualification-attr.csv*, an {{employeeType}} attribute must exist under the additional fields with its value set to {{DEFAULT}} (or another company code):

|qualification_attr_id|qualification_id|attribute_id|operator_code|right_hand_side|
|PERMANENTPROMOS-3-1-SPARK-employeeType|PERMANENTPROMOS-3-1-SPARK|employeeType|EQUALS|DEFAULT|

My assumption is that this attribute is not defined in the base code. The base employee discount promotion likely doesn’t depend on this attribute, which would explain why there isn’t a reference to {{employeeType}} in the standard implementation.

For TVS, a custom dialog is displayed to select the employee type. Once the user selects a type, it’s programmatically added to the {{additionalFields}} map on the {{UserModel}} representing the linked employee.  It is not coming from any user tables.

{{user.setAdditionalField("employeeType", this.defaultCompanyCode.equals(companyCode) ? EMPLOYEE_TYPE_DEFAULT: EMPLOYEE_TYPE_FRG);}}

Because the {{additionalFields}} map isn’t persisted, the {{employeeType}} value is lost when the transaction is supsended.

To address this, I implemented a solution in the customer layer that persists the {{employeeType}} value during suspend and restores it upon resume.

{noformat}@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/transmgmt/suspend", implementation = "tvs-sales")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class TvsSuspendSaleSessionEndpoint {

    private final SuspendSaleSessionEndpoint baseImpl;

    public SuspendSaleSessionResponse suspendSaleSession(SuspendSaleSessionRequest request) {
        RetailTransModel trans = request.getSaleSession().getActiveTransaction();

        /*
         * JMC-1323: Employee Discount not applying when resuming a suspended transaction on it.
         * In order for the employee discount to be triggered as a promotion, the UserModel.getAdditionalFields() map
         * MUST contain the appropriate 'employeeType' value.  This is set in `OnCompanySelect`.  Since the additionalFields
         * hashmap is not persisted, this value gets persisted to RetailTransModel.employeeTypeForDiscount when transaction
         * is suspended and then re-added when the transaction is resumed.
         */
        if (TransactionUtils.hasEmployeeAttached(trans)) {
            addEmployeeTypeToTransModel(trans);
        }

        return baseImpl.suspendSaleSession(request);
    }

    private void addEmployeeTypeToTransModel(RetailTransModel trans) {
        String employeeType = (String) trans.getEmployeeForDiscount().getAdditionalField("employeeType");
        trans.getExtension(TvsRetailTransModel.class).setEmployeeTypeForDiscount(employeeType);
    }

}{noformat}



{noformat}@Endpoint(path = REST_API_CONTEXT_PATH + "/transmgmt/resume", implementation = "tvs-sales")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class TvsResumeSaleSessionEndpoint {
    private final ResumeSaleSessionEndpoint baseImpl;
    private final TransactionManager transManager;

    public ResumeSaleSessionResponse resumeSaleSession(ResumeSaleSessionRequest request) {
        ResumeSaleSessionResponse response = baseImpl.resumeSaleSession(request);

        /*
        * JMC-1323: Employee Discount not applying when resuming a suspended transaction on it.
        * In order for the employee discount to be triggered as a promotion, the UserModel.getAdditionalFields() map
        * MUST contain the appropriate 'employeeType' value.  This is set in `OnCompanySelect`.  Since the additionalFields
        * hashmap is not persisted, this value gets persisted to RetailTransModel.employeeTypeForDiscount when transaction
        * is suspended and then re-added when the transaction is resumed.
        */
        addEmployeeDiscount(response.getSaleSession());

        return response;
    }

    private void addEmployeeDiscount(SaleSession saleSession) {
        RetailTransModel trans = saleSession.getActiveTransaction();
        String employeeType = trans.getExtension(TvsRetailTransModel.class).getEmployeeTypeForDiscount();

        if (employeeType != null && trans.getEmployeeForDiscount() != null) {
            trans.getEmployeeForDiscount().setAdditionalField("employeeType", employeeType);
            transManager.updateAndSaveTransaction(saleSession, false);
        }
    }
}{noformat}



