TVS Raised a following bug:
*Shrug Guy when Combining Receipted and Non-Receipted Return with Customer Attached*

Steps to reproduce the issue:

# Start a transaction with customer attached
# Add a non-receipted return (with an order attached) to the transaction
## As a prerequisite, need to create a sale transaction with a minimum of two line-items where at least one of them is an order line-item.
## To perform non-receipted return, scan the itemID pertaining to non-order item from the mixed transaction created in (a).
## A select screen appears to select a reason code, select any one.
# Shrug guy appears 

Logic Investigation:

Upon investigating the issue, we found out that TVS has a logic for creating the parentOrderID in TvsGetParentOrderIdEndpoint, which sets the parentOrderId as a combination of {{storeNumber + terminal + date + transSequenceNumber + orderSequenceNumber}}. We observed that the {{parentOrderId}} is being generated as a *20-digit string*. When we perform a non-receipted return for a mixed transaction (order + cash-and-carry item), the ReturnTransHelper class has to split the order transactions using {{splitInStoreAndOrderTransactions}} method which has the following logic implemented: 

{noformat}if (StringUtils.isNotEmpty(orderTransaction.getParentOrderId())) {
    orderTransaction.setSequenceNumber(Long.parseLong(orderTransaction.getParentOrderId()));
} else {
    orderTransaction.setSequenceNumber(Long.parseLong(orderTransaction.getOrderId()));
}{noformat}

Java's {{Long}} type can hold a maximum value of {{9,223,372,036,854,775,807}}. This means that our {{parentOrderId}} needs to be *19 digits or less* to avoid exceeding the {{Long}} range. Currently, the first 4 digits of the {{parentOrderId}} represent the store number, which could pose problems for store numbers like {{9710}} or {{9788}}.
Since TVS has business requirement to set the parentOrderId in the format listed above, they would instead like to fix the logic for the ReturnTransHelper class when parsing the parentOrderId.

